/ActualText (Experience\nUI/UX Product Designer \nSpringworks - Dec 2020 - Aug 2026\(Responsibility \nLed end-to-end product design across enterprise web applications, from problem definition and user flows to wireframes, prototypes, high-fidelity UI, and developer handoff.\nPartnered closely with Product and Engineering to shape product requirements, challenge assumptions, and improve usability across complex workflows.\nDesigned data-heavy interfaces and operational workflows, including dashboards, tables, configuration experiences, and multi-step processes.\nWorked with cross-functional teams to establish reusable UI patterns and maintain consistency across product experiences.\n\nKey projects \(Springverify \(Enterprise Background Verification Platform\) \023 Designed complex operational workflows across vendor management, verification, approvals, and AI-assisted experiences, simplifying fragmented processes for Operations and client-facing teams.\(EngageWith \(Employee Engagement Platform\) \023 \nDesigned engaging employee recognition and rewards UI, enhancing user interaction. Created a seamless Slack and Microsoft Teams integration, enabling real-time peer recognition.\nEZ Drafts \(Real Estate Contract Drafting Tool\) \023 \nDefined the product's visual language and designed workflows for creating, managing, and customizing complex real-estate agreements.\(\nUI Designer\nYellowchalk UI/UX Design studio \(Sketch\nOct 2017 - Jun 2020\nDesigned responsive experiences across web and mobile products for clients including Pramata and TeamLease.\nConducted user research and feedback analysis to inform product direction and interaction decisions.\nEstablished and promoted UI guidelines and reusable design patterns across projects.\nCollaborated with Product, and UX teams from wire-framing through implementation.)
/K [6]
